{"content":"0.5c: delete the `effort` argument, so there is no second way to say it. `CommunicateInput.effort` (`crates/kcode-app-core/src/tool/communicate.rs:1757`) and its five pass-throughs (`:1264`, `:1415`, `:2469`, `:2741`, `:2793`), the schema text (`:1969-1972`) and the model-list hint (`:1652`), the wire fields `CommSpawn::effort` (`crates/kcode-protocol/src/wire.rs:500`) and `CommAssignTask::effort` (`:617`), and the `agents.swarm_effort` pin (`crates/kcode-config-types/src/lib.rs:461`, `default` at `:492`, `clap` env override `KCODE_SWARM_EFFORT` at `crates/kcode-base/src/config/env_overrides.rs:306-313`, the template comment `default_file.rs:380`) with `config_tests.rs:276`. The five schema verbs shrink to four after F1 anyway, so the text is touched twice; accepted, 0.5 is kept and the tail is droppable.","status":"pending","priority":"","id":"t3","kind":"implement","assigned_to":"session_nautilus_1790962815996_8fa88cc17ddc5734"}
{"content":"0.5d: name the losses. `docs/what-was-removed.md` records what 0.5 takes, each with why: a repo can no longer pin its spawned workers' level (`agents.swarm_effort`, `KCODE_SWARM_EFFORT` via t3), a coordinator can no longer set a worker's level per call (the tool argument and its wire fields, t3), and a config can no longer set a provider's level (`provider.openai_reasoning_effort`, `provider.anthropic_reasoning_effort`, a named profile's `reasoning_effort`, and `/account openai effort` with it, t7). Each is now the session's level, inherited by what it spawns, and reachable by one human action (`/effort`, the picker, the effort keys, ACP). Also record the default shift of t6 for models that ship a higher one (Opus `xhigh`, fable `high` start at `low` until cycled up).","status":"pending","priority":"","id":"t4","kind":"implement","blocked_by":["t3"],"assigned_to":"session_nautilus_1790962815996_8fa88cc17ddc5734"}
{"content":"0.5's gate: `cargo fmt --all --check`, clippy for `kcode-app-core`/`kcode-base`/`kcode-config-types`/`kcode-protocol`/`kcode-tui` and the provider runtimes with `--all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`, and the full suite via `scripts/test.sh full`, because the resolution order and the spawn inheritance are behavior, not deletion (re-run any flake single-threaded before believing it). Then the live probe on its own socket: a fresh session on a `low`-capable model reports `low`, `/effort high` reports `high` and survives a resume, a worker spawned from it inherits `high`, and a config that still carries `provider.openai_reasoning_effort` or `agents.swarm_effort` starts clean and sets nothing.","status":"pending","priority":"","id":"t5","kind":"verify","blocked_by":["t3","t6","t7"],"assigned_to":"session_nautilus_1790962815996_8fa88cc17ddc5734"}
{"content":"0.5e: the low default lives in the model table, not in config. `default_reasoning_effort_for_model` returns `low` for every model whose ladder accepts it (`kcode-provider-openai-runtime/src/lib.rs:1013` today: only `gpt-5.6-sol` is `low` and everything else is `None`; `kcode-provider-anthropic-runtime/src/lib.rs:738` carries the per-model values), so kcode's shipped intent has one home and per-model exceptions are data. Measured against today: `ProviderConfig.openai_reasoning_effort` is `Some(\"low\")` (config-types:1061) and applies to every OpenAI model at construction (`openai_provider_impl`'s `new_inner`), so the config layer and the table already disagree about OpenAI, and config wins.","status":"pending","priority":"","id":"t6","kind":"implement","assigned_to":"session_nautilus_1790962815996_8fa88cc17ddc5734"}
{"content":"0.5f: config stops setting effort at all. Delete `ProviderConfig.openai_reasoning_effort` and `.anthropic_reasoning_effort` (`crates/kcode-config-types/src/lib.rs:1008`, `:1010`, with the compiled `Some(\"low\")` at `:1061` and `None` at `:1062`) and `NamedProviderModelConfig.reasoning_effort` (`:346`), plus what exists only to serve them: the OpenAI provider's construction read (`kcode-provider-openai-runtime/src/lib.rs:818-823`) and the openrouter per-profile reads, the env override (`crates/kcode-base/src/config/env_overrides.rs:484`), `Config::set_openai_reasoning_effort` (`config_file.rs:130`) and `/account openai effort` with its usage line, help text, suggestion, account-center row (`auth_account_picker.rs:190-196`, `auth_account_commands.rs:239`, `:983`, `input_help.rs:180`, `state_ui_input_helpers.rs:818`), the display summary (`display_summary.rs:185`), the template lines (`default_file.rs:315-320`, and `provider_setup.rs:675`'s generated config), and the tests that assert the keys (`config_tests.rs:128`, `:655-722`, `change_report_tests.rs:117`, the openrouter construction tests).","status":"pending","priority":"","id":"t7","kind":"implement","assigned_to":"session_nautilus_1790962815996_8fa88cc17ddc5734"}
